rue,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.016415495939726382,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":8.2,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5156138827289164,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":14.1,"_gate_incr_roic":0.05875250385287788,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":36.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.04654357747765748,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":17.8,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06431135258712051,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":14.3,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0025255804565616755,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":47.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.019613990638301586,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":19.6,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.03042,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":20.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.214,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":21.4,"pf":[],"description_full":"Constellium SE, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the design, manufacture, and sale of rolled and extruded aluminum products for the aerospace, packaging, automotive, commercial transportation, general industrial, and defense end-markets. It operates through three segments: Packaging & Automotive Rolled Products, Aerospace & Transportation, and Automotive Structures & Industry. The Packaging & Automotive Rolled Products segment produces and develops rolled aluminum products, including canstock and closure stock for the beverage and food industry, as well as foil stock for the flexible packaging market. This segment also supplies automotive body sheets, heat exchangers, and battery foil products for the automotive market. The Aerospace & Transportation segment provides aluminum products including plate, sheet, and extrusions to aerospace, space, commercial transportation, general industrial, and defense sectors. The Automotive Structures & Industry segment offers structural solutions for the automotive industry including crash management systems, body structures, side impact beams, and battery enclosure components; soft and hard alloy extrusions for automotive, transportation, and general industrial applications; and profiles for rail and general industrial applications. This segment also provides downstream technology and services, which include pre-machining, surface treatment, research and development, and technical support services. It sells its products directly or through distributors in France, Germany, the Czech Republic, the United Kingdom, Switzerland, and the United States, as well as South Korea, Japan and China. The company was incorporated in 2010 and is headquartered in Paris, France.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Ingrid  Joerg | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $681K ranks in the above the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $16K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Constellium SE is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $3.0B market cap on $7.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 10% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $183M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.92\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.10438385179213176},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $6.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-6201986.7},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 53% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (CSTM) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_CSTM_That_Institutions_Follow_111026025601_1794340561.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794340561.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Constellium SE (CSTM) \u2013 What Are Investment Firms Thinking About This Stock?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/constellium-se-cstm-what-are-investment-firms-thinking-about-this-stock.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794216557.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Constellium (CSTM) Earnings Strength Keeps The Undervalued Narrative In Play","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-cstm/constellium/news/constellium-cstm-earnings-strength-keeps-the-undervalued-nar","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794134056.587,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"How Strong Quarterly Earnings At Constellium (CSTM) Has Changed Its Investment Story","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-cstm/constellium/news/how-strong-quarterly-earnings-at-constellium-cstm-has-change","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794043724.919,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Constellium (CSTM) Stock May Trade At A Discount As It Raises Full Year Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-cstm/constellium/news/constellium-cstm-stock-may-trade-at-a-discount-as-it-raises","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793953891.281,"origin":"tiingo","s